-- title:
--   Hecke eigenclass over K from an idempotent corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation domain with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $L \ge 1$ and let $S$ be a set of natural numbers. On $H^1(L,\top;\mathcal O) = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L,\top),\mathcal O)$, the additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_H(L,\top) = \Gamma_0(L)$ (the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ cut out by `GammaH L ⊤`) to $\mathcal O$, consider the family `opFamily L ⊤ S 𝒪` indexed by the generators `Gen L S`: the transfer operator $T_\ell$ for each prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, the operator $U_q$ for each prime $q \mid L$, and the diamond operator for each $d \in (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$; assume (hypothesis `hcomm`) that these pairwise commute, and fix an arbitrary $\bar\theta : \mathrm{Gen}(L,S) \to k$. Let $\mathbb T =$ `opSubalgebra` of the resulting `HeckeData`, namely the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1(L,\top;\mathcal O))$ generated by this family, and let $Sp$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb T$: a number $n$, idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ forming a complete orthogonal family, and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_0,\dots,\mathfrak m_{n-1}$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb T$, with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j$ precisely when $i \ne j$. Fix an index $i_0$, write $e = e_{i_0}$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with injective structure map. The assertion is that there exist a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the corner ring $e\mathbb T e$ to $K$ and a non-zero $c \in \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(L),K)$ such that: (i) if every element of the corner submodule $e \cdot H^1(L,\top;\mathcal O)$ satisfies the parabolicity condition of [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62) (vanishing at the relevant elements of $\Gamma_0(L)$), then $c$ satisfies it too; (ii) for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, the transfer operator `heckeT L ⊤ ℓ K` sends $c$ to $\varphi(e\,T_\ell\,e)\cdot c$; and (iii) for every prime $q \mid L$, `heckeT L ⊤ q K` sends $c$ to $\varphi(e\,U_q\,e)\cdot c$. No condition is imposed on $c$ with respect to the diamond operators.
--
--   This is the passage from an occupied local factor of the Hecke algebra acting on the integral cohomology $H^1(\Gamma_0(L),\mathcal O)$ to a single $K$-valued eigenclass whose $T_\ell$- and $U_q$-eigenvalues are read off from a $K$-point of the corresponding corner ring. It is used by [`CohCarrier.exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_apply_T_eq_of_cornerRing_point_of_corner_le_parabolicHoms`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_apply_T_eq_of_cornerRing_point_of_corner_le_parabolicHoms), which repackages the eigencharacter as a homomorphism on the whole Hecke algebra.
-- source:
